Z||000010||Spyder||12-01-2001||08:35 PM||||Thank You, Thank You….*blushing*<BR>I’m very proud.<P>I had bought the interior kit from Specialty Car Interiors a long time ago.  It looks a lot like the 300zx and it does use Nissan trim parts.<P>Rogergarrison: I would love to go to Carlisle but kind of far for me… but… <BR>I’ll be at Daytona this year with her (the car). I’m looking forward to Daytona already.<P>Cheever: let’s put it this way, they know me…<P>DaRkLoRD: on the door panel hook up, not done, but it will hook up just by bending the stock Fiero’s rods.  I’m not sure how I’m going to do them for sure; the doors open by solenoid with door poppers.<P>Here is a pic of the same interior kit done in tan:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/interiora.jpg">  <BR>And here is a pic of how the kit came:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/interiorb.jpg"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||7
